\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Branch summary: every axis measured against the multi-scale, $H_0{+}H_1$, CoordConv starting configuration, at the default $q=0.95$ calibration, $n=10$ seeds per arm unless noted. Vectorization rows are the native-encoder path. $^a$ Rips fails on $10/10$ seeds before training starts, for the degenerate-birth reason given in the text. $^{c}$$n=3$, the only seeds run at the current calibration ($\sigma _{\text  {pixels}}=0.5$); see Section~\ref {ssec:method}. The DTM$_5$ / fused rows support the process-specific scale choice of Section~\ref {ssec:method} rather than ablating a single model.}}{11}{table.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
